P</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAIKIN INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, OSAMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>URAOKA, NOBUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>URAOKA NOBUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>URAOKA, NOBUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An air filter filter medium having a polytetrafluoroethylene porous membrane and an air-permeable support material laminated on at least one surface of the porous membrane, wherein the porous membrane and the support material are bonded together via a fibrous hot-melt adhesive concatenated by independent fibers and/or knots, thereby keeping a high trapping efficiency of an air filter filter medium and a pressure loss as low as that encountered with a fusion bonded one.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un support de filtrage pour filtre à air comportant une membrane poreuse en polytétrafluoroéthylène et un matériau support perméable à l'air laminés sur au moins une surface de la membrane poreuse. Cette membrane et le matériau support sont collés l'un à l'autre au moyen d'un produit adhésif thermofusible fibreux concaténé par des fibres et/ou des noeuds distincts. Ainsi le support de filtrage du filtre à air possède une capacité d'arrêt élevée pour une perte de pression aussi faible que dans le cas d'un assemblage par fusion.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>